NAME
       grub2-install - install the GRUB boot loader on a disk

SYNOPSIS
       grub2-install [OPTION]... DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       grub2-install writes GRUB's first stage to the start of DEVICE (on BIOS
       machines) and copies GRUB's modules into /boot/grub2. It is used to
       repair a machine whose boot loader was damaged or to make a second disk
       bootable. On UEFI machines RHEL 9 boots from the signed shim and GRUB
       files that the shim-x64 and grub2-efi-x64 packages put in /boot/efi:
       do not run grub2-install there, reinstall those packages instead.

       grub2-install does not write the menu. The menu still comes from
       /boot/grub2/grub.cfg and the entries in /boot/loader/entries.

OPTIONS
       --target=PLATFORM
              The platform to install for, such as i386-pc for BIOS machines.

       --boot-directory=DIR
              Install GRUB's files under DIR/grub2 instead of /boot/grub2.

       --recheck
              Forget the saved device map and probe the disks again.

EXAMPLES
       Put GRUB back on the first disk of a BIOS machine:
              # grub2-install /dev/vda
              Installing for i386-pc platform.
              Installation finished. No error reported.

SEE ALSO
       grub2-mkconfig(8), grub2-probe(8), grubby(8)
